 ],
 "literal": "Natural beauty being lost, beauty of the shoulders wasting away, / with a distressed heart, every night without sleeping, / having become pale, will [she] perish indeed? / In the cool, fragrant seaside grove where white herons cry, / scattering the fresh flowers of the flower-abounding thicket, / the transverse waves break. With the lord of such a shore, / to smile so that shining teeth appeared, is this the result?",
 "translation": "Is this the only reward for having smiled, revealing shining teeth, in the company of the lord of the shore, where transverse waves break, scattering the fresh blossoms of the flower-rich thickets in the cool, fragrant seaside grove where white herons cry? Now, her natural beauty is lost, her shoulders have wasted away, and with a distressed heart, she lies awake every night, fading away under a spreading pallor.",
 "modern": "இயற்கையான அழகு அழிந்து, தோள்களின் அழகு மெலிந்து, துன்பப்படும் நெஞ்சத்தோடு இரவெல்லாம் தூங்காமல், பசலை நோய் கொண்டு இறந்து போவதுதானோ—வெண்மையான நாரைகள் ஒலிக்கும் குளிர்ந்த மணமுள்ள கடற்கரைச் சோலையில், பூக்கள் நிறைந்த புதர்களில் உள்ள அன்றைய புதிய மலர்களைக் கலைத்து, குறுக்காக வரும் அலைகள் கரையில் மோதி உடையும் துறைமுகத் தலைவனுடன், விளங்கும் பற்கள் தெரியுமாறு அன்று மகிழ்ந்து சிரித்ததன் பயன்?",
 "explanation": "In this Neytal (maritime) poem, the friend (tōḻi) addresses the heroine, who is suffering deeply from the hero's separation. She questions whether this intense physical and mental decay is the only outcome of the brief moments of joy they shared when they smiled together. The heroine's natural beauty has vanished, her shoulders have wasted away, and she lies awake every night with a distressed heart, covered in the yellow-green spots of pallor (pacalai). The poem uses a vivid maritime image: the transverse waves crash and scatter the fresh blossoms in the flower-rich thickets of the cool, fragrant seaside grove where white herons cry. This natural imagery acts as an implied metaphor (ulluṟai), where the waves breaking the fresh flowers represent the hero's sudden departure shattering the heroine's delicate beauty and happiness.",
